\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Dimension utility over the complete rate grid. (a) Final-state retention after shared random coordinate removal; the zero-removal value is one by definition. (b--d) Native-coordinate margin attribution at all five stages. Each optimizer curve averages all four rates and 14 tasks; (a) additionally averages 20 shared masks per nonzero fraction. The gray curve or horizontal line is the pretrained reference. Lines join measured points, not fitted trajectories. These are descriptive means, not confidence intervals or full-corpus retrieval scores; formal contrasts and rotation controls are reported separately.}}{7}{figure.caption.5}\protected@file@percent }
